# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# A callable held by a field of a nested body is called there: the field is
# of the body that declares it. 100 + 10 + 2. Entry 7.
fn: make2 (int: n) fn: (int: x; int: y) int
    fn: f2 (int: x; int: y) int
        return: n + x * 10 + y
    return: f2
int: c 1
int: ok 81
if: c = 1
    @: h2 make2(100)
    if: h2(1 2) = 112
        ok: 7
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
